From b99b4c0ecc750cdf6b3709cccb87ce73cb68bc5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:38:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(2d): join open contour runs and handle inside corners

Deduplicate XY-coincident picked open runs and weld touching runs end to end in `selection_geometry_impl` so manual edge picks around inside corners offset as continuous chains instead of overrunning adjacent walls. Unify `contour_open` and `contour_run_side` on `offset_run_side`, which keeps the outer sweep boundary past bottleneck notches, classifies acute convex joins via `corner_sector_left`, resolves end-cap ties under arc sag, and drops swallowed normal endpoints on short inside-corner legs.

Fixes #2277
